That is a great UI polish. Since you configured the Amount input text to start typing from the right side, shifting the helper text to the right or center will make it look much more balanced!
You just need to add the textAlign property inside the sx prop of those specific <Typography> tags.
Here is exactly what to change. I will set them to "right" to match your Amount typing direction, but you can easily change the word "right" to "center" if you prefer it exactly in the middle.
### Step 1: Update the Amount Helper Text
**Find this exact line right below your Amount <TextField> (around line 522):**
```javascript
                  <Typography variant="caption" sx={{ fontSize: "0.65rem", color: "text.secondary", mt: 0.5, display: "block" }}>

```
**Replace it with this (adds textAlign: "right"):**
```javascript
                  <Typography variant="caption" sx={{ fontSize: "0.65rem", color: "text.secondary", mt: 0.5, display: "block", textAlign: "right" }}>

```
### Step 2: Update the Product Code Helper Text
**Find this exact line right below your Product Code <TextField> (around line 564):**
```javascript
                  <Typography variant="caption" sx={{ fontSize: "0.65rem", color: "text.secondary", mt: 0.5, display: "block" }}>

```
**Replace it with this (adds textAlign: "right"):**
```javascript
                  <Typography variant="caption" sx={{ fontSize: "0.65rem", color: "text.secondary", mt: 0.5, display: "block", textAlign: "right" }}>

```
Save the file and check your UI. The text will now sit perfectly aligned under the right side of the input boxes! If you decide you want it perfectly in the middle instead, just change "right" to "center" in those two lines.
